    title: 'Signature, customer type and student ID notice',
    markdown:
      '# Signature, customer type and student ID notice (draft)\n\n> **DRAFT — NOT APPROVED FOR PUBLICATION — REQUIRES REVIEW BY A QUALIFIED NIGERIAN LEGAL PROFESSIONAL**\n> Prepared by the engineering team from the behaviour of the application as of 2026-11-01. Square-bracket items are unverified facts or unmade decisions. Nothing here is legal advice, and nothing here has been approved by the owner, AFIT, or counsel. Do not publish.\n\nOperator: [NOBS AGENT — LEGAL NAME, REGISTRATION AND ADDRESS TO BE VERIFIED; not yet registered]. Contact: [AFIT MARKET SUPPORT EMAIL — TO BE PROVIDED].\n\n## 1. Your hand-off signature\n\nWhen you create an account you draw a signature. We keep it and use it for one purpose: when a delivery or pick-up is handed over, the signature drawn on the day is compared with the one you registered. If the two look clearly different, the hand-off is refused so that a parcel is not given to the wrong person. Small differences are expected and are allowed. The comparison is automatic and approximate. It does **not** prove who you are and it is not a legal electronic signature [COUNSEL: confirm wording against the Evidence Act 2011 as amended in 2023].\n\n- **What we store:** the image of your signature, and the date it was registered. Staff cannot view it in normal use. [COUNSEL: decide whether administrators may view it in a dispute, and how that is logged.]\n- **Accounts created before this feature:** you are asked to register a signature the next time you sign in.\n- **Changing it:** [OWNER DECISION: not yet possible without contacting support].\n- **Deleting it:** when your account is erased, the signature is deleted.\n\n## 2. Customer type\n\nWhen you register as a customer you tell us whether you are a student, military, a lecturer or other. This is your own statement. We use it [OWNER TO CONFIRM PURPOSE: for example to prioritise student deliveries or to understand who uses the service]. We do not check it for military, lecturer or other.\n\n## 3. Student ID number and ID card photo\n\nIf you say you are a student we ask for your student ID number and a photo of your ID card (the 2026 version).\n\n- **We do not check the card against any school record.** An administrator may look at the photo and the number and may decide to restrict an account. [COUNSEL: confirm that this limited use is described accurately and is lawful.]\n- **Where it is kept:** the number is encrypted. The photo is stored privately and can only be opened by an administrator. Each time an administrator opens it, the access is recorded in the audit log.\n- **Sensitive content:** an ID card photo can show a face and other personal details. [COUNSEL: advise whether this is "sensitive personal data" under the NDPA, whether explicit consent is needed, and the retention period.]\n- **Deletion:** erased with your account.\n\n## 4. Consent text shown at sign-up\n\n"I understand that my signature will be compared with the signature I draw when a delivery or pick-up is handed over, and that my student ID number and ID card photo (students only) are kept privately and may be looked at by AFIT Market staff."\n\n[COUNSEL: confirm this is enough, or whether a separate tick box is needed.]\n',
