    markdown:
      "# Vendor Agreement (draft)\n\n> **DRAFT — NOT APPROVED FOR PUBLICATION — REQUIRES REVIEW BY A QUALIFIED NIGERIAN LEGAL PROFESSIONAL**\n> Prepared by the engineering team from the behaviour of the application as of 2026-11-01 (updated from the 2026-10-13 version). Square-bracket items are unverified facts or unmade decisions. Nothing here is legal advice, and nothing here has been approved by the owner, AFIT, or counsel. Do not publish.\n\nBetween [NOBS AGENT — LEGAL NAME, REGISTRATION AND ADDRESS TO BE VERIFIED; not yet registered] (the operator) and the vendor named at application. Support: [AFIT MARKET SUPPORT EMAIL — TO BE PROVIDED].\n\n## 1. Onboarding and verification\n\nThe vendor applies with business name, phone, category, description and pickup location, and accepts this agreement. The operator may verify identity and contact details and may approve, reject or later suspend a vendor, giving reasons. [OWNER/COUNSEL: acceptable ID for individuals; registration number for businesses; payout-account verification before any payout exists; the application today collects none of these and does not verify the phone.]\n\n## 2. Permitted and prohibited products\n\nOnly products allowed by the operator's list may be sold. [OWNER: list not yet written.] Food vendors must meet applicable food-safety rules [COUNSEL: which authority and licences].\n\n## 3. Listings, prices, availability and preparation times\n\nThe vendor is responsible for accurate descriptions, prices (in naira) and availability and for honest preparation times. Orders are fulfilled as accepted.\n\n## 4. Fulfilment and handover\n\nThe vendor accepts, prepares and marks orders ready and hands over to the customer (pickup, using the one-time code) or to the assigned rider. Handover is recorded in the app.\n\n## 5. Commission and what you receive\n\nAFIT Market keeps a commission of **4.5% of the product value of each completed order** (the order's product subtotal after any product discount). **Delivery fees are not part of the commission base.** The commission is shown to you per order on your Earnings page before and after refunds. If part of an order is refunded, the commission on that part is returned to you; amounts are calculated in whole kobo, rounding half up. The rate in force when an order completes is saved with that order and does not change for it later. Of the commission, AFIT Market allocates 3% to itself and 1.5% as an internal budgeting allowance toward payment-provider charges; **the allowance is not a statement of what the provider charges, and AFIT Market pays the actual provider charges.** The customer pays no extra platform fee. [COUNSEL: confirm wording, whether the split should be disclosed to vendors at all, and treatment of VAT or other taxes.]\n\n## 6. Delivery fees\n\nCustomers pay delivery fees through the app. The delivery fee is not part of the commission base. [OWNER: whether any part reaches the vendor; currently none.]\n\n## 7. Payout calculation and timing\n\n[OWNER/COUNSEL/PAYSTACK: not defined. Vendor settlement is locked and no payout exists; do not state a timetable.]\n\n## 8. Refunds, disputes and incorrect items\n\nThe vendor cooperates with complaints, returns and eligible refunds under the Refund, Return and Dispute Policy. Where a customer is refunded because of vendor fault, [OWNER: who bears the cost].\n\n## 9. Records\n\nThe vendor keeps records the law requires [COUNSEL/TAX].\n\n## 10. Privacy\n\nThe vendor uses customer information only to fulfil the order. [COUNSEL: controller/processor roles and NDPA obligations of the vendor.]\n\n## 11. Suspension, termination and appeal\n\nSuspension or removal follows a notice stating reasons, a chance to respond, and a review by someone other than the first decider. [OWNER.]\n\n## 12. Law\n\n[COUNSEL: governing law, disputes, indemnities, limits.]\n\n## Payout account (added 2026-11-01)\n\n- The shop owner chooses a bank and enters an account number. The service asks the payment provider for the account name the bank has on file and shows it in capital letters. The owner confirms by tapping Verify.\n- Once verified, the account **cannot be changed** unless the owner contacts customer service, who may unlock it after a check. Each unlock is recorded with a reason.\n- The account number is stored encrypted; staff see only the last four digits.\n- Being verified does not mean any payout has been made or is promised. [COUNSEL: payout timing and conditions, holdbacks for disputes, and what happens when the account name differs from the registered business name.]\n",
